# Gemini-Powered UI Automation Framework

This repository contains a Playwright-based UI testing framework augmented with Google's Gemini model via Vertex AI. It supports traditional `pytest` tests, AI-generated selectors, and LLM-directed execution through LangChain.

---

## 📁 Project Structure

```
ai_ui_test_framework/
├── src/
│   ├── ai_adk/              # AI selector and MCP agent logic
│   ├── pages/               # Page Object Models
│   ├── tests/               # Pytest test cases
│   ├── utils/               # Config, fixtures, reporting
│   └── features/            # Cucumber feature files and steps
├── ci/                      # CI/CD config
├── requirements.txt
└── vertex_prompt_schema.yaml
```

---

## 🧪 Features
- AI-enhanced selector generation using Google AI ADK
- Gemini-pro LLM via LangChain to control browser actions
- Dual-mode testing: `pytest` and `behave` (Cucumber-style)
- Screenshot capture on failure
- Cloud-native ready (Vertex AI, GCP BigQuery logging supported)

---

## 🔧 Setup Instructions

### 1. Create and activate a virtual environment
```bash
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate  # On Windows: venv\Scripts\activate
```

### 2. Install dependencies
```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
playwright install
```

### 3. Set Vertex AI credentials
Export your service account key:
```bash
export GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS="path/to/your-service-account.json"
```

### 4. Run tests
- Standard Pytest:
```bash
pytest src/tests
```
- Cucumber-style (Behave):
```bash
behave src/features
```

